DTEND;TZID=America/New_York:20261105T230000
SUMMARY:Ashley Monroe & Charlie Worsham
LOCATION:The Bitter End\, Greenwich Village
DESCRIPTION:Ashley Monroe is one of Nashville's most respected and influent
 
ial voices whose work has helped shape modern country music from the inside
 
 out. Over a career spanning nearly 25 years\, she's earned GRAMMY nominati
 
ons\, widespread critical acclaim\, and the admiration of her peers through
 
 both her solo catalog and her work with Pistol Annies. Her recent music ma
 
rks a bold new chapter of creative clarity and emotional honesty. On her su
 
rprise-released album Dear Nashville\, written and produced alongside Luke 
 
Laird\, Monroe turns inward\, exploring her complicated relationship with t
 
he town that built her. The eight-song concept album captures the tension b
 
etween deep love for country music and the emotional toll of the industry\,
 
 delivered with the unfiltered perspective that has long defined her songwr
 
iting. With more new music continuing to emerge\, Monroe remains as vital a
 
s ever---an artist still evolving\, still telling the truth\, and still fin
 
ding new ways to be heard. Twenty years after moving to Nashville\, Charlie
 
 Worsham has established himself as one of Music City's most respected arti
 
sts: a singer-songwriter\, producer\, award winning instrumentalist\, podca
 
st host\, and collaborator. With Once Upon a Second Time Around\, he reflec
 
ts on a life he once dreamed of and realizes he is already living it. Raise
 
d in Mississippi on bluegrass\, country\, and rock & roll\, Worsham brings 
 
those influences together in a deeply personal album shaped by marriage\, f
 
atherhood\, friendship\, and personal growth. Created after stepping away f
 
rom the major-label system\, the project embraces creative freedom and auth
 
enticity over commercial expectations. Rather than chasing trends\, Worsham
 
 focused on crafting a complete album centered on strong songwriting\, musi
 
cianship\, and honest performances. The songs explore gratitude\, resilienc
 
e\, and second chances\, ranging from intimate acoustic moments to expansiv
 
e bluegrass and southern rock arrangements. A two-time ACM Acoustic Guitar 
 
Player of the Year and the 2024 CMA Musician of the Year\, Worsham delivers
 
 his most personal work yet: an album that celebrates growth\, perspective\
 
, and appreciating what is already in front of him. Please Note: All Sales 
 
Final. Two Item Minimum Per Attendee. 18+ admitted if accompanied by parent
 
 or guardian. Tickets & info: https://www.ticketweb.com/event/ashley-monroe
 
-charlie-worsham-the-bitter-end-tickets/14995573
URL:https://www.ticketweb.com/event/ashley-monroe-charlie-worsham-the-bitte
 
r-end-tickets/14995573
END:VEVENT
